      en: "The National Assembly of São Tomé and Príncipe (Assembleia Nacional) is the unicameral legislative body of the republic, housed in a prominent building in the capital. Often referred to as the Palace of Congresses (Palácio dos Congressos), the complex is the epicenter of political power and the site of critical democratic debate. Here, 55 deputies convene to pass legislation and exercise oversight over the government's executive actions. The architecture presents a blend of post-colonial design and modern functionality. As the seat of the legislature, the building is highly secured, yet it plays a public role during state visits and formal official ceremonies. It stands as a testament to the parliamentary democracy established following the constitutional reforms of 1990.",
